configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.allowDefaults=Allow Defaults
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.allowDefaults.tooltip=While enabled, this setting allows a default set of blocks to be fluidloggable.\nOther mods can also have internal fluidlogging blacklist/fluidTag/whitelist configs while this setting is enabled.\nIf this setting is changed, you must run the "/fluidlogged reload" command.\n§eThe full set of default fluidloggable blocks added by Fluidlogged API can be viewed on its source page, linked below (click anywhere)\nhttps://github.com/jbredwards/Fluidlogged-API
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.bucketFluidlogging=Bucket Fluidlogging
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.bucketFluidlogging.always=Always
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.bucketFluidlogging.noSneak=No Sneak
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.bucketFluidlogging.onSneak=On Sneak
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.bucketFluidlogging.tooltip=This setting controls how sneaking affects the player's ability to fluidlog blocks with a bucket.\n- Always: Players are always able to fluidlog blocks, regardless of whether they're sneaking. This is the Vanilla 1.13+ behavior.\n- No Sneak: Players cannot fluidlog blocks while sneaking. This is the legacy Fluidlogged API (pre-v3.0.0) behavior.\n- On Sneak: Players can only fluidlog blocks while sneaking.
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.downloadModConfigs=Online Config Mode
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.downloadModConfigs.disabled=Disabled
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.downloadModConfigs.ignoreUpdates=Ignore Updates
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.downloadModConfigs.keepUpdated=Keep Updated
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.downloadModConfigs.tooltip=If this setting is changed, you must run the "/fluidlogged reload" command.\nThis setting controls how the online configs are handled.\n- Disabled: Prevents Fluidlogged API from updating its internal online config cache, and prevents it from being used in-game.\n- Ignore Updates: Prevents Fluidlogged API from updating its internal online config cache, but still allows the existing cache to be applied in-game.\n- Keep Updated: Allows Fluidlogged API to keep its internal online config cache up-to-date, and allows it to be applied in-game.\n§eSee the following link for more info (click anywhere)\nhttps://github.com/jbredwards/Fluidlogged-API-Configs
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision=Fancy Fluid Collision Mode
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.always=Always
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.medium=Medium Entities
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.never=Never
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.players=Player Entities
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidEntityCollision.tooltip=While enabled, fluid blocks have significantly more accurate collision with entities.\n- Never: Fancy fluid collision is never applied.\n§2  - Performance impact: None\n- Player Entities: Only apply fancy fluid collision to player entities.\n§2  - Performance impact: Little to None\n- Medium Entities: Only apply fancy fluid collision to medium-sized entities (whose bounding box has no side greater than 3 blocks).\n§2  - Performance impact: Small to Medium\n- Always: Universally apply fancy fluid collision to all entities (this should never be used).\n§2  - Performance impact: Small to Very Large
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidRenderer=Fancy Vanilla Fluid Rendering
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fancyFluidRenderer.tooltip=While enabled, force water and lava to use the same fluid renderer that modded fluids use.\nThis setting has a medium performance impact, but this can almost always be mitigated by using certain performance mods, like CensoredASM, Nothirium, and VintageFix.\n§eThis setting should only be disabled as a last resort, as it fixes MANY bugs, primarily:\n- MC-4533: §7§oWater and lava graphical glitch when connecting diagonally\n- MC-100886: §7§oFalling sand with an ID of water or lava does not render\n- MC-127030: §7§oWater and lava attempt to connect to fluidlogged blocks when they shouldn't, causing several issues\n- MC-127270: §7§oVisual water and lava level inside fluidlogged blocks do not adjust correctly\n- MC-227302: §7§oSmooth lighting does not work properly on the water surface
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fixBadFluidMixing=Fix https://bugs.mojang.com/browse/MC-127108
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fixBadFluidMixing.tooltip=While enabled, waterlogged blocks cannot turn lava into obsidian or cobblestone on physically unconnected sides.\nThis fix is also applied to many modded fluid interactions. Please submit a bug report to Fluidlogged API's issue tracker if you find any incompatible mods!
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fluidStateIsFireInsulator=Fluids Protect Against Fire
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.fluidStateIsFireInsulator.tooltip=While enabled, flammable blocks cannot ignite while fluidlogged with fireproof fluids.
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.ignoreLowFluidCollision=Prevent Shallow Fluid Swimming
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.ignoreLowFluidCollision.tooltip=While enabled, non-aquatic entities cannot swim in shallow fluids (like in Vanilla 1.13+).\nThis setting stacks with "Fancy Fluid Collision Mode", and has no performance impact while enabled.
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable=Lava Vaporizing Mode
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.always=Always
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.flammable=Any Flammable
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.fluidloggable=Flammable and Lavaloggable
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.never=Never
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.lavalogVaporizeFlammable.tooltip=While enabled, any lava-like fluid (has the lava material) flowing into a flammable block will cause the block to be vaporized.\n- Never: This setting is disabled.\n- Flammable and Lavaloggable: Only vaporize blocks that can be fluidlogged with lava, and that are flammable.\n- Flammable: Only vaporize blocks that are flammable. Note that these blocks don't have to be fluidloggable.
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.nonSourceFluidlogging=Non-Source Fluidlogging
configgui.fluidloggedAPI.general.nonSourceFluidlogging.tooltip=While enabled, allow fluids that are not source blocks to be fluidloggable.

